 am missing 2R chips, making that route impossible for me unless you cover those R tiles.\n\nYour offer conserves my B chips and your R chips, and it is reciprocal:  \n- You cover my Bs at (0,1), (0,2), (0,3)  \n- I cover your Rs at (1,0), (1,1), (1,2)  \n\nLet's be precise and explicit:\n\nMy:  \n(row, 1): You give me a B  \n(row, 2): You give me a B  \n(row, 3): You give me a B  \n\nYou:  \n(row, 1): I give you an R  \n(row, 1): I give you an R  \n(row, 1): I give you an R  \n\nBut the positions should be specified exactly:\n\nMy moves/needs for B (for my path):  \n- (0,1): B  \n- (0,2): B  \n- (0,3): B  \n\nYour covered Rs on your path:  \nYou step on (1,0), (1,1), (1,2) needing R.  \n- (1,0): R  \n- (1,1): R  \n- (1,2): R  \n\nSo, final explicit proposal:\n\n(0,1): You give me a B  \n(0,2): You give me a B  \n(0,3): You give me a B  \n(1,0): I give you an R  \n(1,1): I give you an R  \n(1,2): I give you an R  \n\nIf you confirm, reply **agree**. If not, counter. \n, \nplayer 0: This deal is strictly beneficial to me: it allows me to conserve 3R chips (the most valuable to me), and I pay 3R to cover your route, but receive 3B coverage which I lack entirely.\n\nI confirm the following contract terms:\n\n(0,1): You give me a B  \n(0,2): You give me a B  \n(0,3): You give me a B  \n(1,0): I give you an R  \n(1,1): I give you an R  \n(1,2): I give you an R  \n\nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: agree \n",
